# Vulnerability details

## Impact
A borrower can add themselves as an authorized lender allowing them to both `borrow` and `deposit` into the market.

This will allow a borrower to completely drain a market of all its assets circumventing the `Reserve Ratio` put in place.

It also allows the borrower to have a senior claim on any potential assets paid back by a 3rd party leaving any honest lender with no option to be paid back through the contract. Protocol fees can still be claimed in case of a white knight effort to pay back debt, not making the protocol look good in the eyes of honest lenders.

It should not be possible for a borrower to get more money out of a market than was intended.

