## **Impact**

If a user sees in the mempool that the borrower wants to borrow money, he can frontrun him by calling `queueWithdrawal()` and DOS the borrowing operation. This can be very annoying for the borrower.

From a game theory perspective, every lender is incentivized to behave this way because

1. even in the withdrawal queue, the lender's stake is still earning interest,
2. when the payoff happens, he will be in the withdrawal queue and will be prioritized over the others,
3. and if the borrower needs to borrow money, he probably can't refund the market right now, so the malicious user will stay in the queue and earn interest for a moment.

