# Vulnerability details

## Impact
Function values can run out of gas, leading to a DOS. The amount of unpaid withdrawals in the queue is incremented when function value() is called. but there is no check to stop the loop in values(), This loop can take all the gas limit and If the gas limit is reached, calls to the function will fail or revert.

```
  function values(FIFOQueue storage arr) internal view returns (uint32[] memory _values) {
    uint256 startIndex = arr.startIndex;
    uint256 nextIndex = arr.nextIndex;
    uint256 len = nextIndex - startIndex;
    _values = new uint32[](len);

    for (uint256 i = 0; i < len; i++) {
      _values[i] = arr.data[startIndex + i];
    }

    return _values;
  }
```

