The contract adds unpaid withdrawals to a queue by using a first-in-first-out pattern in batches. The shift function removes data from the array by deleting the first index from the array, If the queue gets too long, the gas cost for deleting startIndex would make it impossible to delete. This can lead to a dos and make the contract to not work as expected.

```
  function shift(FIFOQueue storage arr) internal {
    uint128 startIndex = arr.startIndex;
    if (startIndex == arr.nextIndex) {
      revert FIFOQueueOutOfBounds();
    }
    delete arr.data[startIndex];
    arr.startIndex = startIndex + 1;
  }
```

## Tools Used
Manual Review

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
Add a check to prevent the queue from becoming too long. For example,  let it revert after a certain length e.g startIndex + 10.






