## Summary

There are two conditions that lead to the possibility that paying protocol fees can be avoided and borrower and/or lenders save/earn funds by doing so:

1. The protocol allows arbitrary ERC-20 tokens and protocol fees are paid in these tokens
2. As the borrower must authorize the lender address, they both must know each other / must communicate with each other

This enables the possibility that they both agree on using a special wrapper contract as ERC-20 token which allows to 1:1 swap for another token like for example USDC, but has a special transfer function which does not transfer funds to the feeRecipient of the protocol and instead split it between the borrower and the lender for example.

