# Vulnerability details

The WildcatMarkets are designed to detect delinquency when saving their state, without looking back on how debt and reserves evolved over time. Grace periods and delinquency fees are then calculated starting from the moment when delinquency is detected, rather than when it happened.

## Impact
Borrowers who deal with lenders who rarely interact with the protocol can abstain from interacting with the protocol too, and profit from un-processed delinquency status for potentially long periods of time. Delinquency can be avoided altoghether by front-running state-changing interactions with just repayments.

## Proof of Concept
The following PoC shows how a borrower that would normally be delinquent for 1 year is not required to pay any delinquency fees:

```Solidity
    function testQueuedWithdrawal() public {
        // we start with a market with
        // - 1% reserve ratio
        // - 10% annual interest
        // - 100% delinquency fee

        // lender deposits
        vm.startPrank(lender);
        uint256 amt = 100e18;

        token.mint(lender, amt);
        token.approve(address(market), amt);

        market.deposit(amt);

        // borrower borrows everything they can
        // so we expect them to become immediately delinquent
        uint t0 = block.timestamp;
        vm.startPrank(borrower);
        market.borrow(99e18);

        // however, after 1 year, they repay their debt
        // **without** delinquency fees;
        // this would normally not be enough
        // to cover the extra delinquency fees
        vm.warp(t0 + 365 days);
        token.mint(address(market), 109e18);
        market.updateState();

        // ...but it is, because there are no delinquency fees
        assertFalse(market.isDelinquent());
    }
```

